WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:04.430
We regret to inform you that Skyscraper has
collapsed.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:09.240
Pitched as "Die Hard meets The Towering Inferno,"
the Dwayne Johnson-led action movie premiered

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:14.180
to a significantly lower-than-expected financial
reception, coming out of its first weekend

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.040
in third place at the box office.

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:20.610
As a result, the would-be franchise starter
will be lucky to make its money back, much

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.490
less spark a new series.

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.680
More likely than not, you can forget about
a sequel already.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:30.000
So why is this disaster movie proving to be
such a… disastrous movie?

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:31.780
Could the Rock's star be fading?

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:33.550
Is the movie actually that bad?

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.530
Let's tally up the numbers and figure out
the real reasons Skyscraper couldn't stand

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:40.489
tall at the box office.

00:00:40.489 --> 00:00:41.899
What's the damage?

00:00:41.899 --> 00:00:46.390
According to a breakdown by The Hollywood
Reporter, Skyscraper only managed a domestic

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:50.690
total of $25.5 million in its opening weekend.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:56.559
The unexpectedly small take falls below Universal's
projected opening of $30 million or more.

00:00:56.559 --> 00:01:02.230
Against a budget of more than $125 million
and a marketing budget of at least half that,

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:07.110
those numbers are a pretty poor showing, one
which Box Office Mojo predicts will translate

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:11.140
into a $65 to $75 million domestic total.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:15.440
Since these projected earnings wouldn't even
cover half of Skyscraper's total cost, that

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:20.640
leaves a huge deficit to bridge in the international
market, just for the sake of breaking even.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:26.000
But with only $40.4 million coming in from
the movie's global audience on opening weekend,

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.540
the chances of even that happening are looking
vanishingly small.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:31.450
I think I've seen this

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:35.880
If Skyscraper feels too familiar to be all
that interesting, that's actually partially

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:36.880
by design.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.310
Prior to the movie's release, Johnson described
the movie on his social media as "a film that

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:46.670
paid homage and respect to the classic action
movies that inspired me and entire generations

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:50.210
- Die Hard to Towering Inferno to The Fugitive."

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:53.800
The thing about those classic action movies
is not just that we've seen them before, but

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.150
that we've also already seen them all get
ripped off.

00:01:56.150 --> 00:02:00.370
We've seen Cliffhanger, we've seen Speed,
we've seen Daylight - and they all feel a

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:01.940
lot like Skyscraper.

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:06.200
So as much as Johnson and the movie's producers
would like to praise Skyscraper as a modern

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:09.270
classic, it's not a quality that feels all
that earned.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:13.409
It doesn't help that Skyscraper comes off
as feeling similar to some of Dwayne Johnson's

00:02:13.409 --> 00:02:18.310
other recent movies, from San Andreas to Rampage
to even The Fate of the Furious.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:22.249
But that's not this movie's problem - that
speaks to issues with the movie's marquee

00:02:22.249 --> 00:02:23.989
star.

00:02:23.989 --> 00:02:24.989
Over-exposed

00:02:24.989 --> 00:02:30.849
Over a 14-month span starting in April 2017,
Dwayne Johnson has been a lead star in five

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:35.370
different movies, including Baywatch, Jumanji,
and now Skyscraper.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:39.269
The avalanche of content shows no signs of
stopping, but it might already be bringing

00:02:39.269 --> 00:02:40.650
in diminishing returns.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:45.860
In short, Johnson has opened himself up to
the possibility of serious overexposure.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:50.099
With no less than ten movies potentially coming
down the pipeline for the actor, you'd have

00:02:50.099 --> 00:02:53.980
to be crazy not to think that we're at risk
of some serious Rock fatigue.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:57.379
If it can happen to Star Wars, it can happen
to the People's Champion.

00:02:57.379 --> 00:03:01.650
Could Skyscraper's failure inspire Johnson
to tone down the full-court press?

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:02.650
Maybe.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:06.530
After all, how is the country ever going to
elect him president if everyone's burned out

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.579
on his movies?

00:03:08.579 --> 00:03:09.639
The competition

00:03:09.639 --> 00:03:14.560
Whatever its own faults may be, Skyscraper
was also outmatched at the box office by more

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:16.480
critically acclaimed competition.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:21.150
On one side, there's Hotel Transylvania 3:
Summer Vacation, another entry in the Adam

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:24.620
Sandler-starring animated series about Dracula
and friends.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:30.200
That family-friendly sequel won the weekend
with $45 million, easily trouncing Skyscraper's

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.319
debut showing.

00:03:31.319 --> 00:03:35.170
In second place, there's Ant-Man and the Wasp,
with nearly $29 million.

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:39.400
According to both Rotten Tomatoes scores and
Cinemascores, people walked out of these two

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:43.379
movies feeling satisfied, and ready to spread
some positive word of mouth.

00:03:43.379 --> 00:03:47.930
To its detriment at the box office, Skyscraper
is proving more divisive, and without good

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:52.689
word of mouth behind it, things are only going
to get worse from here.

00:03:52.689 --> 00:03:53.719
Catch it later

00:03:53.719 --> 00:03:57.650
So does Skyscraper really deserve this belly-flop
of a reception?

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:58.950
Well, yes and no.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:02.669
Put simply, Skyscraper is not the kind of
appointment viewing that makes you want to

00:04:02.669 --> 00:04:07.040
schlep out to the cinema, regardless of how
bombastic its special effects might be.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.459
Instead, it's the kind of thing you see accidentally,
killing time with an in-flight movie while

00:04:11.459 --> 00:04:12.459
you're on a plane.

00:04:12.459 --> 00:04:17.420
Multiple reviews emphasized the movie's nature
as something slight and inessential - enjoyable

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.530
enough as a nice diversion, but not good for
much else.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:24.920
In a crowded movie landscape, "good enough"
often doesn't cut it - not when other movies

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.780
are competing for the same audience.

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:31.360
In these days of razor-thin profit margins,
sometimes that's all you need to make a box-office

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:31.860
bomb.

